section__
  @title "Sunspear Prison Confession with steel drawn"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/00-prologue-core/frame-018.jpg"

  "In Sunspear's guest crypt, a captive confessor trades names for water: couriers paid by three competing factions, a planned poisoning at a neutral feast, and a ledger hidden under a false chapel floor. He speaks with split lips and desperate precision. The chamber smells of damp stone, orange peel, and old incense.

If the confession is true, exposing it now could prevent a massacre and collapse two alliances at once. If planted, acting on it could frame Valehart as a butcher of guests and oathbreakers. Torture has made lies and truth wear the same face, and you must still issue orders before sunrise.

You record every name, every place, and every contradiction. In this war, intelligence is never clean. It is merely timely or late."

